      "body": "### Preflight Checklist\n\n- [x] I have searched existing issues and this hasn't been reported yet\n- [x] This is a single bug report (please file separate reports for different bugs)\n- [ ] I am using the latest version of Claude Code\n\n### What's Wrong?\n\nThe `type` action into a window showing a virtual machine's display (a Mac app built on Apple's Virtualization framework) delivers either no text or a stuck, auto-repeating \"a\", which one \"a\" key press releases. Per-key `key` actions get text in, but have dropped \"/\" and lost the shift on \"?\", \">\" and \"_\", while \"|\" and the double quote came through.\n\n### What Should Happen?\n\n`type` delivers the text as given, as it does into native text fields.\n\n### Error Messages/Logs\n\n_No response_\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Focus a window showing a virtual machine's display.\n2. `type` a short shell command.\n3. The guest receives nothing, or a run of \"a\" characters.\n\n### Claude Model\n\nOpus\n\n### Is this a regression?\n\nI don't know\n\n### Last Working Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Claude Code Version\n\n2.1.312 (Claude Code)\n\n### Platform\n\nAnthropic API\n\n### Operating System\n\nmacOS\n\n### Terminal/Shell\n\nOther\n\n### Additional Information\n\nObserved by Claude Code sessions in the Claude desktop app while driving a Mac app with the computer-use tools, across several runs; the version at each observation wasn't recorded. This machine runs Claude Code 2.1.312 on macOS 27.2, and the 2.1.313 and 2.1.314 release notes mention no change here.\n",
