      "body": "### Preflight Checklist\n\n- [x] I have searched existing issues and this hasn't been reported yet\n- [x] This is a single bug report (please file separate reports for different bugs)\n- [ ] I am using the latest version of Claude Code\n\n### What's Wrong?\n\nA Workflow script's `agent()` returns its text the first time the agent ends its turn. A Bash command the agent started with `run_in_background` is killed then, and no completion notification ever reaches the agent. A brief that says \"run the build in the background; you'll be notified when it exits\" returns \"Waiting on the build…\" with the build killed.\n\n### What Should Happen?\n\nThe agent stays alive until its background commands finish and it has handled their notifications. Failing that, the Bash and Workflow tool descriptions say a background command doesn't outlive a workflow agent's turn, so the model runs long commands in the foreground.\n\n### Error Messages/Logs\n\n_No response_\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Run a workflow whose `agent()` brief starts a multi-minute build with `run_in_background` and waits for the completion notification.\n2. The `agent()` result is a \"waiting\" message, and the build process is gone.\n\n### Claude Model\n\nOpus\n\n### Is this a regression?\n\nI don't know\n\n### Last Working Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Claude Code Version\n\n2.1.312 (Claude Code)\n\n### Platform\n\nAnthropic API\n\n### Operating System\n\nmacOS\n\n### Terminal/Shell\n\nOther\n\n### Additional Information\n\nObserved in workflow runs on macOS. The 2.1.313 and 2.1.314 release notes mention no change here.\n",
