      "body": "### Preflight Checklist\n\n- [x] I have searched existing issues and this hasn't been reported yet\n- [x] This is a single bug report (please file separate reports for different bugs)\n- [ ] I am using the latest version of Claude Code\n\n### What's Wrong?\n\nScreen-level clicks in roughly the top 90 pt of a display, where the menu bar and window toolbars are, can be dropped in every app, while clicks lower down and hover still work. A full-screen Claude window at window layer 1000, invisible in screenshots, sits over that display.\n\n### What Should Happen?\n\nClicks on the menu bar and on window toolbars reach them.\n\n### Error Messages/Logs\n\n_No response_\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. During full-screen computer-use control, click a window's toolbar button or a menu-bar item.\n2. Nothing happens, while the same control responds to `app_click` (an accessibility press) or `app_menu`.\n\n### Claude Model\n\nOpus\n\n### Is this a regression?\n\nI don't know\n\n### Last Working Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Claude Code Version\n\n2.1.312 (Claude Code)\n\n### Platform\n\nAnthropic API\n\n### Operating System\n\nmacOS\n\n### Terminal/Shell\n\nOther\n\n### Additional Information\n\nWorkaround: press the control with `app_click` or `app_menu`.\n\nObserved by Claude Code sessions in the Claude desktop app while driving a Mac app with the computer-use tools, across several runs; the version at each observation wasn't recorded. This machine runs Claude Code 2.1.312 on macOS 27.2, and the 2.1.313 and 2.1.314 release notes mention no change here.\n",
