      "body": "### Preflight Checklist\n\n- [x] I have searched existing issues and this hasn't been reported yet\n- [x] This is a single bug report (please file separate reports for different bugs)\n- [ ] I am using the latest version of Claude Code\n\n### What's Wrong?\n\nWith the computer-use tools on macOS, a modifier held with `hold_key` is released before the next action in the same batch. A menu that shows an item only while Option is held therefore can't be screenshotted with that item showing.\n\n### What Should Happen?\n\nA key held with `hold_key` stays down for the actions that follow it in the batch, so an Option-only menu item can be shown and screenshotted.\n\n### Error Messages/Logs\n\n_No response_\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. In one batch: `hold_key` Option, click a menu-bar menu that has Option-only items, and take a screenshot.\n2. The screenshot shows the menu without its Option-only items.\n\n### Claude Model\n\nOpus\n\n### Is this a regression?\n\nI don't know\n\n### Last Working Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Claude Code Version\n\n2.1.312 (Claude Code)\n\n### Platform\n\nAnthropic API\n\n### Operating System\n\nmacOS\n\n### Terminal/Shell\n\nOther\n\n### Additional Information\n\nWorkaround: Option-click the base item, then confirm what it opened.\n\nObserved by Claude Code sessions in the Claude desktop app while driving a Mac app with the computer-use tools, across several runs; the version at each observation wasn't recorded. This machine runs Claude Code 2.1.312 on macOS 27.2, and the 2.1.313 and 2.1.314 release notes mention no change here.\n",
