      "body": "### Preflight Checklist\n\n- [x] I have searched existing issues and this hasn't been reported yet\n- [x] This is a single bug report (please file separate reports for different bugs)\n- [ ] I am using the latest version of Claude Code\n\n### What's Wrong?\n\nIn a batch that drags, a `mouse_move` that lands on an ungranted app's window is refused, and the tool lets go of the mouse button there, so the drag drops early at that point. Computer-use screenshots hide such windows, so the path looked clear.\n\n### What Should Happen?\n\nA refused step leaves the mouse button as it was, or ends the batch without releasing it at that point, and the result says the drag was cut short.\n\n### Error Messages/Logs\n\n_No response_\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Leave an ungranted app's window on screen between a draggable item and its target.\n2. In one batch: press the mouse on the item, `mouse_move` across that window, `mouse_move` to the target, and release.\n3. The item drops where the refused step was.\n\n### Claude Model\n\nOpus\n\n### Is this a regression?\n\nI don't know\n\n### Last Working Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Claude Code Version\n\n2.1.312 (Claude Code)\n\n### Platform\n\nAnthropic API\n\n### Operating System\n\nmacOS\n\n### Terminal/Shell\n\nOther\n\n### Additional Information\n\nObserved by Claude Code sessions in the Claude desktop app while driving a Mac app with the computer-use tools, across several runs; the version at each observation wasn't recorded. This machine runs Claude Code 2.1.312 on macOS 27.2, and the 2.1.313 and 2.1.314 release notes mention no change here.\n",
