      "body": "### Preflight Checklist\n\n- [x] I have searched existing issues and this hasn't been reported yet\n- [x] This is a single bug report (please file separate reports for different bugs)\n- [ ] I am using the latest version of Claude Code\n\n### What's Wrong?\n\nScreenshots from the computer-use tools leave out the Claude desktop app's own windows, but those windows stay on screen, cover what is under them, and take clicks. A click or drop aimed at what a screenshot shows can land on a Claude window instead. During full-screen control, the session's own window floats over part of the display and the user can't move it.\n\n### What Should Happen?\n\nEither screenshots show the Claude windows that cover the screen, so the model can see what its clicks will hit, or clicks and drops aimed at what a screenshot shows reach the app it shows.\n\n### Error Messages/Logs\n\n_No response_\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Leave a Claude window overlapping part of the app under test.\n2. Take a computer-use screenshot: the overlapped part shows the app under test.\n3. Click a control in that part: the click lands on the Claude window.\n\n### Claude Model\n\nOpus\n\n### Is this a regression?\n\nI don't know\n\n### Last Working Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Claude Code Version\n\n2.1.312 (Claude Code)\n\n### Platform\n\nAnthropic API\n\n### Operating System\n\nmacOS\n\n### Terminal/Shell\n\nOther\n\n### Additional Information\n\nSeen again today: a Claude window covered the right edge of the app under test, where the controls being tested were, and could not be moved, so the run moved the app's window by script instead. `screencapture -x` does show the Claude window.\n\nObserved by Claude Code sessions in the Claude desktop app while driving a Mac app with the computer-use tools, across several runs; the version at each observation wasn't recorded. This machine runs Claude Code 2.1.312 on macOS 27.2, and the 2.1.313 and 2.1.314 release notes mention no change here.\n",
